## 6. Skills

Plugin-resident skills (installed once; triggered by slash command or the `Skill` tool):

| Skill | Trigger | What it does |
|-------|---------|--------------|
| Close Task | `/close-task` | Step-10 closer: append chronicle, overwrite context_snapshot, status-sync `TODO.md`, conditional `architecture.md` re-audit, rebuild INDEX, move the ticket to Done + Completion Notes. **Every variant runs the kb-curator (if enabled) to fold session knowledge into `docs/knowledge_base/`.** The chronicle + snapshot + KB + INDEX *are* the persisted memory. Variants: full / research / transitory multi-session. With `agents.linear_steward` on (Linear tracker), the linear-steward tidies the closing ticket's project after the kb-curator. |
| Log Activity | `/log-activity` | The single logger. Append-only JSONL writer: one record per lifecycle step → `docs/activity_log.jsonl` (contract: `LOG_FIELDS` / `EVENTS` in `corpus.config.mjs`). With `--tracker`, the same call also posts the mirrored {{TRACKER}} comment cross-referenced by id and applies state markers — reserve it for milestones (Step 1 start, blockers, decisions, Step 10 close). Never moves a ticket to Done. Commits are not logged — `git log` is their record. |
| Council | `/council` | 7-step multi-agent deliberation for contested / architectural / irreversible decisions. The devils-advocate is a mandatory participant. Writes a council doc with explicit reopen criteria. |
| New Doc | `/new-doc` | Scaffolds a governed `.md` (spec, alpha_test, report, review_*, council, handoff) with valid frontmatter from `docs/_templates/`, then validates. |
| Audit Corpus | `/audit-corpus` | Frontmatter validation across all governed `.md` + rebuild `INDEX.md`/`index.json` + a tiered (High/Medium/Low) health report to `docs/audits/`. High findings include sealed alpha tests modified after sealing. |
| Handshake | `/handshake` | Two-machine transfer (`out` / `in` / auto-detect), transport-aware per `handshake.transport`: **synced-folder** = transitory close + sync-verification + marker; on arrival conflict-scan, git integrity, environment verification. **git-remote** = `wip(<TICKET>):` transport commit + handoff doc + push; on arrival ff-pull + snapshot regeneration + verification. Never force-push, never stash, never transports secret values, never mutates machine config without confirmation. |

